From 20ddaafb427d0d8d770c30e157d505b78a7d817e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:18:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Asuswrt-Merlin 3006.102.10 carries: wanduck, WPS PIN, httpd
 guards, IPsec, LLMNR, mounts, Time Machine, libdisk, minidlna

Fixes from Eric "Merlin" Sauvageau's 3006.102.10 alpha 2 (29 commits over
3006.102.9, GPL merge 0c5d53820c), each read against the Reaper tree before
it was taken:
- wanduck: FD_CLR(sfd) before the close, "Host:" parsed past the colon and
  whitespace, gai_strerror on resolver errors, a NULL target guarded. The
  "set_disconn_count only when switch_wan_line succeeds" refinement is NOT
  taken: switch_wan_line() returns 0 when the target is already primary,
  which would skip the reset and reopen the GT-BE98 fail-back loop.
- services.c wl_wpsPincheck(): digits only. "0;reboot" parsed as 0 with a
  valid checksum and reached the hostapd_cli command line (ASUS GPL 102_40585).
- httpd web.c: eight upload handlers walk value = strstr(p, "\r\n\r\n") + 4
  only when strstr() found it; nvram_check() guards a NULL str2;
  validate_apply() guards its two NULLs; the Main_AdmStatus SystemCmd route
  is removed (the page is not shipped; system_cmd_test is an extern in the
  prebuilt web_hook.o, left alone).
- firewall.c: IPSEC_DROP_SUBNET_ICMP uses lan_netmask instead of a /24.
- wsdd2 llmnr.c: the loop entry is bounded.
- common.c check_mountpoint(): getline() instead of a fixed buffer (stack
  overflow on \040-escaped labels) and the fclose leak.
- timemachine.c, libdisk disk_io_tools.c + disk_share.c, minidlna upnpsoap.c
  + tagutils-dff.c: upstream verbatim.
Not carried, by design: httpd no_cache max-age (drops no-store), the
VUPNP/FUPNP re-add, unconditional core dumps, the Instant Guard INPUT
insert, the WireGuard kill-switch rework, forced pause on ethernet ports.

web.c also carries ej_wlpro_nvram()'s parse of wlN_chanfit_st for the
Wireless page (whole-file grouping; it belongs with the node-fit commit).

Host suites 72 pass / 2 skip, static checks 14/14. Metal: owner RT-BE96U
v3.4.5_BETA_r7..r9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
